<div class="container masterplan">

<h1 id="top">Schema System Plan — W0.1 detail</h1>

<div class="last-updated doc-muted">
    Created: 2026-08-24 &nbsp;|&nbsp; Version: 1.0 &nbsp;|&nbsp; Status: ACTIVE (schema branch)
</div>

<p>This is the detailed breakdown of MASTER_PLAN's <strong>W0.1 — Schema System Plan</strong>, and the
schema-branch portion of the consolidated <a href="/Documentation/SchemaMasterPlan">SchemaMasterPlan</a>.
It defines the work THIS branch owns. Plans that belong to other branches (AccountingPostgresMigrationPlan / ACCPG,
AccountingOnboardingPlan / ACCON) are <strong>not</strong> authored here — they are tracked as todos for their owners
(see <a href="#blocking">§6 Blocking</a>).</p>

<div class="notice">
    <strong>Why this plan exists.</strong> Every other plan's schema work (Voice Inspection columns, 3D showcase flag,
    Inventory §8 columns, the Maria→PG clone) currently depends on a coherent schema mechanism. Today that mechanism is
    half-done: <code>Util::SchemaCompare</code> exists and <code>/admin</code> endpoints work via DDL-from-Result, but the
    primary/backup resolution is unresolved, raw SQL still lives in <code>Admin/SchemaComparison.pm</code>, and there is no
    drift guard. Until G0+G1 land, other plans cannot safely add columns.
</div>

